.TH HASHTERM 1 "August 2026" "hashterm 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hashterm \- tmux\-native GUI terminal with saved sessions and a quake\-style drop\-down
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hashterm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hashterm
is a frameless, tabbed terminal for Linux built on GTK4/VTE. Every tab is a
session on a dedicated private tmux server, so terminals survive GUI crashes
and detaches. Sessions can be fully dumped (layout, working directories,
running programs, scrollback) and restored later, browser\-style.
.PP
The window behaves as a quake\-style console: a global hotkey (default
\fBF12\fR) slides it from the screen edge and keeps it above other windows.
Tabs are organized as a two\-dimensional \fImatrix\fR: groups (rows) on one
window edge, the active group's terminals (columns) on the perpendicular
edge.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Use an alternative configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Toggle the drop\-down terminal of the running instance (or start one).
.TP
.B \-\-restart
Replace the running GUI with a fresh instance (e.g. after an upgrade). Your
terminals live on the tmux server, which stays up, so they are re\-adopted and
nothing is lost.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-tab
Open a new tab in the running instance.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " DIR"
Working directory for \fB\-\-new\-tab\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-restore " NAME"
Restore a named saved session in the GUI ("latest" resolves to the newest
autosave).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exec " \fICMD\fR..."
Command to run in the new tab; consumes all following arguments.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dump \fINAME\fR
Headless full dump of the dedicated tmux server (also used internally by tmux
hooks and the autosave timer).
.TP
.B restore \fINAME\fR
Headless restore of a named save onto the dedicated tmux server.
.TP
.B saves
List saved sessions.
.SH KEYS
Defaults (all configurable in \fI[hotkeys]\fR):
\fBF12\fR toggle drop\-down;
\fBCtrl+Shift+T\fR new tab; \fBCtrl+Shift+W\fR close tab;
\fBCtrl+Home\fR/\fBEnd\fR previous/next terminal;
\fBCtrl+PgUp\fR/\fBPgDn\fR previous/next group;
\fBAlt+1..0\fR jump to tab;
\fBCtrl+Shift+B\fR toggle tab bar; \fBCtrl+Shift+S\fR session picker;
\fBCtrl+Shift+C\fR/\fBV\fR copy/paste;
\fBCtrl+Alt+Shift+scroll\fR window opacity (remembered across restarts).
Right\-click a tab or a group row for properties, group moves, rename and
group color. Drag a tab onto another tab to reorder, onto a group row to move
it there, onto the group bar's \fB+\fR to move it into a new group.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hashterm/config.toml
Configuration; live\-reloaded on save. A fully commented reference is written
here on first start.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hashterm/user.css
Extra GTK CSS overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hashterm/
Saved sessions (dumps, autosaves) and UI state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The dedicated tmux server runs on socket \fBhashterm\fR
(\fItmux \-L hashterm\fR attaches to it directly if needed).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1)
